    "created_at": "2021-09-09T08:08:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-09T17:10:03Z",
    "body": "Exposing the current status of other modules to custom modules is not possible in our current architecture. The reason is that the modules are executed in parallel so we won't know which modules to set as active when the custom modules are executed. That said what it looks like you are asking for is a way to tell if you are in a git repo or not, finding the repo root is done before the modules are executed so this could be something we could expose in the custom modules, maybe as an env var. ",
